# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Why this exists: this project is edited from both Windows and macOS, and
# QLC+ rewrites the whole .qxw on every save using platform line endings.
# Normalization currently happens to work because this machine's
# core.autocrlf handles it, but that is per-machine config, not a property
# of the repo - a clone on a differently-configured machine would start
# committing CRLF and turn every one-scene change into a whole-file diff.
#
# With `text` set here, Git normalizes CRLF -> LF on `git add` regardless of
# local config, so it no longer matters what QLC+ or a Mac editor wrote.

* text=auto

# QLC+ workspaces and fixture definitions are XML - always text.
*.qxw text
*.qxf text

# Wavefront OBJ/MTL are ASCII.
*.obj text
*.mtl text

# The UI build must be byte-reproducible, or the CI guard that rebuilds it and
# diffs against the committed copy cannot tell "someone forgot to rebuild" from
# "this checkout has different line endings".
#
# Two separate problems, both caused by `* text=auto` above:
#
#   * ui/index.html is INPUT to vite. Checked out as CRLF on Windows, vite treats
#     the stray CR as page content and emits it plus its own newline, so the
#     built index.html gets \r\r\n and a fresh Windows clone can no longer
#     reproduce the committed bundle. Pinning the web sources to LF fixes it at
#     the source rather than papering over it in the comparison.
#   * ui/dist is OUTPUT. Normalizing a build artifact is meaningless -- nothing
#     ever hand-edits it -- and it makes every byte comparison platform-specific.
ui/index.html text eol=lf
ui/src/** text eol=lf
ui/*.json text eol=lf
ui/*.ts text eol=lf
ui/dist/** -text

# GDTF is a ZIP container; Blender scenes and renders are binary.
*.gdtf binary
*.blend binary
*.blend1 binary
*.ply  binary
*.glb  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
